Hi all,

This is to announce that sysstat 8.0.1 has been released and is 
available for download. This is a *stable* version.

In this version the pidstat command has been greatly improved with the 
addition of a new option that enables it to display statistics for every 
thread managed by the system.

Sysstat 8.0.1 is available for download from my web page at:
http://perso.orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

207kB sysstat-8.0.1.tar.gz
165kB sysstat-8.0.1.tar.bz2
210kB sysstat-8.0.1-1.src.rpm
165kB sysstat-8.0.1-1.i586.rpm

It will also be available on ibiblio Linux archive site in a few days:
ftp://ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/system/status/

The sysstat utilities are a collection of performance monitoring tools 
for Linux. These include sar, sadf, mpstat, iostat, pidstat and sa 
tools. Check out http://perso.orange.fr/sebastien.godard/features.html
to get a view of sysstat's main features.
Feedback always welcomed. Send your remarks and comments to:
sysstat <at> orange <dot> fr.

To learn some more about sysstat, check out
http://perso.orange.fr/sebastien.godard/

Enjoy!

Changes vs 8.0.0 are:
* Option -t added to pistat. pidstat can now display stats for every 
thread (TID) of a process.
* pidstat's option -T CHILD now reports global statistics for selected 
tasks and all their children (and not only for the children).
* pidstat now reads VSZ and RSS values from /proc/#/stat instead of 
/proc/#/status.
* Fixed a rare parallel make issue creating archive libsyscom.a [GENTOO 
bug #193208].

